      },
      "worked": "Let $u=2^x>0$. Then $8^x=u^3$ and $4^{x+1}=4u^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u^3+u&=4u^2\\\\u^2+1&=4u\\\\u^2-4u+1&=0\\\\u&=\\frac{4\\pm\\sqrt{16-4}}{2}\\\\u&=2\\pm\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are positive, so both give real solutions.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\log_2(2+\\sqrt3)\\text{ or }\\log_2(2-\\sqrt3).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
